1
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:04,400
Here's the bag.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,700
Will he be OK, Dad?

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:11,600
I hope so.

4
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:12,900
That's it.

5
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:13,900
That's the way.

6
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:17,100
That's it. There.

7
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:20,500
Oh, it's going to be all right.

8
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,000
That's it.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,700
Wrap him in the blanket, Dad!

10
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,200
That's it. That's it.

11
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,100
It's all right, Albert.

12
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:30,700
You're going to be OK.

13
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:31,700
I want my daddy!

14
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,100
We'll take you to him.

15
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:41,100
Easy now. Easy does it. That's it.

16
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:42,400
Your dad is quite a guy.

17
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,900
I know, Grandpa.

18
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:46,100
How is he, Philip?

19
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:47,700
He's asleep.

20
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:48,500
He's going to be fine.

21
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,100
How can I thank all of you?

22
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,600
Thank my son Robbie.

23
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,700
He pulled him out of the water.

24
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,500
I'm very grateful, Robbie.

25
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:56,000
Dad saved him, not me.

26
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,600
I'm so thankful to all of you.

27
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,400
So long.

28
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:04,700
He's a lucky boy.

29
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:07,460
Well, what do you say we get back to our fishing?

30
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:09,300
That's a great idea.

31
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:15,000
Uh-oh. It's probably the hospital.

32
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,800
I have to get to a phone.

33
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:19,900
It probably means we can't stay.

34
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:26,700
That's OK.

35
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:29,100
One of my patients has a high fever,

36
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,800
and I have to go to the hospital.

37
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:32,500
I'm sorry, Robbie.

38
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:35,100
I guess I ruined your day.

39
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:41,600
You didn't ruin my day, Dad.

40
00:01:41,600 --> 00:02:10,400
I understand. I really do.

41
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,000
Why are you back so early?

42
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,900
Philip had to go back to the hospital.

43
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:15,600
He had an emergency.

44
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:17,800
Oh, that's too bad, Robbie.

45
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,800
Did it spoil your fun?

46
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,500
No, Mom. We had a great time.

47
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:23,800
Well, did you do any fishing?

48
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:30,200
Yeah, we caught lots of them. Look!

49
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,700
They had a special on frozen fish down at the supermarket.

50
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:37,000
Oh, you really had a bad day.

51
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,100
We had a good day.

52
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:41,700
Robbie pulled a boy out of the water.

53
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:44,500
And Dad saved his life.

54
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,200
He's a terrific doctor, Mom.

55
00:02:47,200 --> 00:03:00,300
I know.

56
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:02,400
Hi, Pop. Hi, Son.

57
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,600
Hello, Dad.

58
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,300
What a day!

59
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:08,400
How about a cup of coffee, Son?

60
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:17,400
I'd love a cup of coffee.

61
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:19,100
How was the patient?

62
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:21,100
She'll be fine.

63
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:23,430
Was it serious?

64
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:26,100
No.

65
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:30,200
Until today, I was never really interested in medicine.

66
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,900
Well, it's hard work.

67
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:35,400
Now I know.

68
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:38,500
I had a good time today, Robbie.

69
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:41,200
Me, too.

70
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,000
Why don't we do it again?

71
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,600
Can we? When?

72
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,600
How about next Saturday?

73
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:50,200
Won't you be busy?

74
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:53,600
I'm changing my schedule.

75
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,800
Well, do we have a date?

76
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:57,700
We sure do, Dad.

77
00:03:57,700 --> 00:03:59,380
Grandpa, can you come?

78
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:02,700
I have other plans, Robbie.

79
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:06,100
But I think you two can have a good time together without me.

80
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:09,100
No, Dad, and certainly not without the right magic.
